;; Continuous coverage loop for the worldwide community corpus held in the
;; com-junkawasaki superproject (90-docs/community-coverage/, ADR-2607257200).
;;
;; Register/ensure with:
;;   COM_JUNKAWASAKI_ROOT=/Users/junkawasaki/github/com-junkawasaki \
;;     bin/tamaki loop ensure --spec loops/community-coverage.edn
;;   COM_JUNKAWASAKI_ROOT=... bin/tamaki loop list
;;   COM_JUNKAWASAKI_ROOT=... bin/tamaki loop tick --max 1
;;
;; The per-iteration protocol is NOT in this file. It is versioned with the
;; corpus at 90-docs/community-coverage/iteration-runbook.edn, so the runbook
;; and the data it governs move together. This spec only points at it.
{:loop/id :community-coverage/worldwide
 :loop/enabled true
 :loop/description
 "Raise coverage of worldwide communities — local, sport, fraternal, union,
  international, traditional, net-native — explicitly including organizations
  that are probably not legally registered. One iteration adds 4-6 forms,
  pins at least one to a real source when the web is reachable, and updates
  ADR-2607257200's current-state block."
 :loop/tags #{:community-coverage :corpus :coverage :unregistered :continuous}
 :loop/objective
 "READ 90-docs/community-coverage/iteration-runbook.edn FIRST and follow it
  exactly; it is the authoritative protocol and it overrides any generic
  improve-the-repo instinct. This corpus is documentation, not code: do not add
  tests, do not refactor, do not touch manifest/west.yml (a correct iteration
  leaves it with a zero diff).

  One iteration: (1) run the coverage reporter (default, regions, unpinned,
  integrity) and read the numbers; (2) pick a gap, preferring the regions the
  reporter shows as thinnest, and grep the existing files to confirm the form
  is not already recorded — duplicate :org/id has happened; (3) write ONE new
  90-docs/community-coverage/community-orgs-<theme>-<n>.edn with 4-6 entities
  in the exact attribute shape of the existing files; (4) pin at least one
  entity to a real, dated, attributable source via web search, and if the web
  is unreachable in this environment, ship the entities unpinned as
  llm-recall-unverified rather than inventing a citation; (5) rewrite the
  current-state block of 90-docs/adr/2607257200-worldwide-community-coverage-corpus.edn
  in place with the measured numbers, adding a numbered finding only when
  something structurally new was actually observed; (6) verify — the integrity
  check must print 'clean' and manifest/edn-query.cljs count must still parse —
  before committing; (7) commit in a worktree outside the superproject, push
  the branch in its own command, and merge server-side with gh api merges. No
  rebase, no force-push.

  Invariants that matter more than throughput: never present a recalled number
  as a measurement; every entity states :org/member-count-basis including why
  it cannot be counted; reach, registrations, wallet addresses and cumulative
  memberships never go in :org/member-count but in :org/proxy-metric with their
  bias named; 'searched and not found' is a result worth recording; when two
  sources disagree keep the precise attributable one and record the
  disagreement rather than averaging; record harm and exclusion as part of the
  description; and for communities where being counted is itself the hazard,
  record the form and do not seek rolls. A smaller honest iteration beats a
  larger one with a fabricated figure in it."
 :loop/project "."
 :loop/workspace-env "COM_JUNKAWASAKI_ROOT"
 :loop/continuous true
 :loop/interval-ms 1800000
 :loop/max-cycles 10
 :loop/max-failures 4
 :loop/auto-approve true
 :loop/organism-name "CommunityCoverage"
 :loop/runners ["claude" "claude-zai" "codex"]}
